# Snyk (https://snyk.io) policy file, patches or ignores known vulnerabilities.
version: v1.25.1
# ignores vulnerabilities until expiry date; change duration by modifying expiry date
ignore:
  SNYK-JAVA-ORGJETBRAINSKOTLIN-2393744:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          CVE-2020-29582: This vulnerability relates to information exposure via
          creation of temporary files (via Kotlin functions) with insecure
          permissions. Corda does not use any of the vulnerable functions so it
          not susceptible to this vulnerability.
        expires: 2029-08-01T01:00:00.000Z
        created: 2024-05-30T10:37:19.923Z
  SNYK-JAVA-ORGGRADLE-5750785:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          CVE-2023-35947: This is a build-related vulnerability that does not
          affect the running of Corda. The Gradle build for Corda does not
          unpack any TAR archives. Corda is not exposed to this vulnerability.
        expires: 2029-08-01T01:00:00.000Z
        created: 2024-05-30T10:37:24.413Z
  SNYK-JAVA-COMGOOGLEGUAVA-20825054:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          CVE-2026-102554: This vulnerability relates to unbounded array allocation
          when Java-deserializing Guava's CompactHashMap, CompactHashSet and
          MapMakerInternalMap, which can lead to an OutOfMemoryError when a crafted
          serialization stream is deserialized. The Corda Node and Corda Firewall
          install a JVM-wide Java serialization filter (ObjectInputFilter) at
          startup that rejects deserialization of all non-whitelisted classes,
          including Guava types. Corda uses its own AMQP serialization for P2P and
          RPC messaging and Kryo for checkpoints, neither of which uses Java
          serialization. Corda is therefore not susceptible to this vulnerability.
        expires: 2029-08-01T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-JAVA-ORGECLIPSEJETTY-21243592:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          CVE-2026-18660: This is an issue in Jetty's proxy, where the host
          whitelist/blacklist is matched case-sensitively, allowing hosts that
          differ only by case to bypass the filter (SSRF). Corda only uses Jetty
          in tests and test/development tooling, none of which ship in the
          released Corda Enterprise node or firewall artifacts, and Corda does
          not use Jetty proxy host whitelists/blacklists. Production nodes use
          Artemis/AMQP for P2P and RPC, so an external attacker would not be
          able to exploit this.
        expires: 2029-08-01T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-JAVA-ORGECLIPSEJETTY-21243523:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          CVE-2026-76182: This is an issue in Jetty's TryPathsHandler and
          TryFilesFilter, where reserved characters in the URI path are not
          escaped when forwarding to a template URI, allowing query parameter
          injection. Corda does not use TryPathsHandler or TryFilesFilter, and
          only uses Jetty in tests and test/development tooling, none of which
          ship in the released Corda Enterprise node or firewall artifacts.
          An external attacker would not be able to exploit this.
        expires: 2029-08-01T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-JAVA-ORGOW2ASM-21715452:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          CVE-2026-110260: This vulnerability relates to excessive memory
          allocation in ASM's MethodWriter (computeAllFrames and
          computeMaxStackAndLocal) when processing a crafted class file containing
          thousands of overlapping exception handlers with COMPUTE_FRAMES or
          COMPUTE_MAXS. Within Corda, ASM is used only by the AMQP ClassCarpenter
          in corda-serialization, which generates simple data classes (fields,
          constructor, getters) from fixed bytecode templates. The generated
          bytecode never contains exception handlers, and Corda does not read or
          rewrite external class files with ASM. Remote parties can only influence
          class, field and type names via the AMQP schema, not the bytecode
          structure, so Corda is not susceptible to this vulnerability.
        expires: 2029-08-01T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-JAVA-ORGOW2ASM-21715439:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          CVE-2026-110261: This vulnerability relates to excessive CPU consumption
          in ASM's MethodWriter.computeAllFrames() when a crafted class file with
          methods that cause slow fix-point convergence is processed using
          COMPUTE_FRAMES. Within Corda, ASM is used only by the AMQP ClassCarpenter
          in corda-serialization, which generates simple data classes (fields,
          constructor, getters) from fixed bytecode templates with no loops or
          complex control flow. Corda does not read or rewrite external class
          files with ASM, and remote parties can only influence class, field and
          type names via the AMQP schema, not the bytecode structure, so Corda is
          not susceptible to this vulnerability.
        expires: 2029-08-01T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-JAVA-ORGOW2ASM-21715442:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          CVE-2026-110257: This vulnerability relates to excessive memory
          allocation in ASM's ClassReader.readBootstrapMethodsAttribute() when
          parsing a crafted class file. Within Corda, ASM is used only by the AMQP
          ClassCarpenter in corda-serialization to generate classes with
          ClassWriter. Corda does not parse class files with ASM's ClassReader, so
          Corda is not susceptible to this vulnerability.
        expires: 2029-08-01T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-JAVA-ORGOW2ASM-21715448:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          CVE-2026-110258: This vulnerability relates to excessive memory
          allocation in ASM's Label.addSubroutineRetSuccessors() when processing a
          crafted class file containing multiple RET instructions for a single
          JSR subroutine. Within Corda, ASM is used only by the AMQP ClassCarpenter
          in corda-serialization, which generates classes from fixed bytecode
          templates that never contain JSR or RET instructions (these instructions
          are not permitted in modern class file versions). Corda does not read or
          rewrite external class files with ASM, so Corda is not susceptible to
          this vulnerability.
        expires: 2029-08-01T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-JAVA-ORGOW2ASM-21715445:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          CVE-2026-110263: This vulnerability relates to uncontrolled recursion in
          ASM's SignatureReader.parseType() when parsing a crafted class file with
          a deeply nested generic Signature attribute, leading to a
          StackOverflowError. Within Corda, ASM is used only by the AMQP
          ClassCarpenter in corda-serialization to generate classes with
          ClassWriter. Corda does not use ASM's SignatureReader or parse external
          class files with ASM, so Corda is not susceptible to this vulnerability.
        expires: 2029-08-01T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z
patch: {}
